<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sydir Bilyi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1735–1788</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sydir Bilyi (1735–1788) was a Zaporozhian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> officer who, after the destruction of the Zaporozhian Sich in 1775, became the first ataman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/host-of-loyal-zaporozhians">Host of Loyal Zaporozhians</a> formed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grigory-potemkin">Grigory Potemkin</a> in 1787. He led the Cossacks in the Russo-Turkish War and was mortally wounded in 1788 in fighting near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ochakiv">Ochakiv</a>. The host later became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> Cossack Host.</p></div>
